Reverse an Array

Exercise:
Reverse an array without using .reverse().

Example:

Input:  [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

Output: [5, 4, 3, 2, 1]


Solution:

1. With new Array

const num = [3, 7, 2, 9, 4];
const newArr = [];

for (let i = num.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
  newArr.push(num[i]);
}

console.log(newArr);


2. Inplace without modifying the original Array


const num = [3, 7, 2, 9, 4];
const newArr = [...num].reverse();

console.log(newArr);
console.log(num);


